    answer:
      'A bid tabulation (bid tab) is a side-by-side comparison of the bids received for one scope of work — a supplier package, a sub-tier trade, a rental — showing each bidder’s price and what it does and does not include. Leveling is the step that makes the prices comparable: adding the cost of anything a bidder excluded so every column carries the same scope. The result is a leveled total per bidder and a defensible reason for the award.',
